      "id": "s004",
      "no": 4,
      "source": "The fallacy of composition fails to allow for how the different “parts” interact with each other—if, for example, your efficient administrator and your highly skilled head of IT each assumes the other is in charge of collating prototype test results, then you have a problem.",
